# Inserting and deleting characters and lines (ICH, DCH, IL, DL, DECIC, DECDC), insert mode and REP.

test ICH inserts blanks and pushes the rest right
spec VT510 ICH: blank characters are inserted at the cursor, the cursor stays, text moves right and what passes the margin is lost; xterm ctlseqs CSI Ps @
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[1;3H\e[2@
screen
|ab  cdefgh|
cursor 1,3

test ICH defaults to one blank
spec VT510 ICH default Pn = 1
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[1;3H\e[@
screen
|ab cdefghi|

test ICH with a huge count blanks the rest of the row
spec VT510 ICH: characters scrolled past the right margin are lost
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[1;3H\e[99@
screen
|ab        |

test DCH deletes characters and pulls the rest left
spec VT510 DCH: the remaining characters between the cursor and the right margin move left, blanks are added at the margin
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[1;3H\e[2P
screen
|abefghij  |
cursor 1,3

test DCH defaults to one character
spec VT510 DCH default Pn = 1
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[1;3H\e[P
screen
|abdefghij |

test DCH with a huge count deletes to the end of the row
spec VT510 DCH: if Pn is greater than the number of characters between the cursor and the right margin DCH only deletes the remaining ones
known-fail: alacritty – DCH with a count past the end of the row blanks the whole row, not just from the cursor
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[1;8H\e[99P
screen
|abcdefg   |

test IL inserts a blank line and pushes the rest down
spec VT510 IL: lines below the cursor move down, lines scrolled off the page are lost
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;1H\e[L
screen
|A|
| |
|B|
|C|
cursor 2,1

test IL inserts several lines
spec VT510 IL
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;1H\e[2L
screen
|A|
| |
| |
|B|

test IL with a huge count blanks to the bottom
spec VT510 IL
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;1H\e[99L
screen
|A|

test IL does not feed the history
spec VT510 IL: lines scrolled off the page are lost
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[1;1H\e[L
screen
| |
|A|
|B|
|C|
scrollback-len 0

test DL deletes a line and pulls the rest up
spec VT510 DL: lines below the cursor move up, blank lines are added at the bottom of the scrolling region
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;1H\e[M
screen
|A|
|C|
|D|
| |
cursor 2,1

test DL deletes several lines
spec VT510 DL
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;1H\e[2M
screen
|A|
|D|

test DL with a huge count blanks to the bottom
spec VT510 DL: if Pn is greater than the lines remaining DL deletes only the remaining lines
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;1H\e[99M
screen
|A|

test IL inside a region only moves the lines of the region
spec VT510 IL: lines below the cursor and in the scrolling region move down
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;3r\e[2;1H\e[L
screen
|A|
| |
|B|
|D|

test DL inside a region only moves the lines of the region
spec VT510 DL: lines below the cursor and in the scrolling region move up
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;3r\e[2;1H\e[M
screen
|A|
|C|
| |
|D|

test IL below the region does nothing
spec VT510 IL: no effect outside the page margins
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;3r\e[4;1H\e[L
screen
|A|
|B|
|C|
|D|

test DL above the region does nothing
spec VT510 DL: no effect outside the scrolling margins
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[2;3r\e[1;1H\e[M
screen
|A|
|B|
|C|
|D|

test insert mode pushes characters right
spec VT510 IRM: new characters move characters in page memory to the right; xterm ctlseqs CSI 4 h
size 10 4
feed abcdef\e[1;3H\e[4hXY
screen
|abXYcdef|
cursor 1,5

test insert mode loses what is pushed off the row
spec VT510 IRM: characters moved past the right border are lost
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[1;3H\e[4hX
screen
|abXcdefghi|

test replace mode overwrites
spec VT510 IRM reset: new characters replace the character at the cursor
size 10 4
feed abcdef\e[4h\e[4l\e[1;3HXY
screen
|abXYef|

test REP repeats the last character
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI Ps b: repeat the preceding graphic character
size 10 4
feed a\e[3b
screen
|aaaa|
cursor 1,5

test REP defaults to one repeat
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI Ps b (default = 1)
size 10 4
feed a\e[b
screen
|aa|

test REP wraps like typed text
convention the repeated characters are written as typed ones are: wrapping at the margin
size 10 4
feed abcdefghi\e[3b
screen
|abcdefghii|
|ii|
cursor 2,3

test DECIC inserts columns
spec VT510 DECIC: columns between the cursor and the right margin move right
known-fail: alacritty – DECIC and DECDC (CSI Ps ' } and ' ~) are ignored
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\r\nabcdefghij\r\nabcdefghij\r\nabcdefghij\e[1;3H\e[2'}
screen
|ab  cdefgh|
|ab  cdefgh|
|ab  cdefgh|
|ab  cdefgh|
cursor 1,3

test DECDC deletes columns
spec VT510 DECDC: the remaining columns move left, blank columns are added at the right margin
known-fail: alacritty – DECIC and DECDC (CSI Ps ' } and ' ~) are ignored
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\r\nabcdefghij\r\nabcdefghij\r\nabcdefghij\e[1;3H\e[2'~
screen
|abefghij  |
|abefghij  |
|abefghij  |
|abefghij  |
cursor 1,3

test DL does not feed the history
convention lines deleted by DL are lost, as those IL pushes off the bottom are; the VT510 text for DL says the lines below move up and says nothing of saving the deleted ones, and only a scroll feeds the history
known-fail: alacritty – DL at the top of the screen puts the deleted line into the history
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD\e[1;1H\e[M
screen
|B|
|C|
|D|
| |
scrollback-len 0

test ECH ends a pending wrap
convention xterm clears the wrap flag when it changes the line under the cursor ("with the right part cleared, we can't wrap"): the next character lands where the erased one was
known-fail: alacritty – the wrap stays pending after ECH: the next character wraps
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[Xk
screen
|abcdefghik|
cursor 1,10

test ICH ends a pending wrap
convention xterm clears the wrap flag when it changes the line under the cursor
known-fail: alacritty – the wrap stays pending after ICH: the next character wraps
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[@k
screen
|abcdefghik|

test DCH ends a pending wrap
convention xterm clears the wrap flag when it changes the line under the cursor
known-fail: alacritty – the wrap stays pending after DCH: the next character wraps
size 10 4
feed abcdefghij\e[Pk
screen
|abcdefghik|

test SL shifts the columns left and blanks come in at the right
convention ECMA-48 SL (xterm ctlseqs CSI Ps SP @, default 1) moves the data Ps columns left; here the columns between the margins of every line in the scrolling region move, and the cursor stays where it is
known-fail: alacritty – no SL or SR (CSI SP @, CSI SP A)
size 8 3
feed abcdefgh\r\nABCDEFGH\e[2 @
screen
|cdefgh|
|CDEFGH|
cursor 2,8

test SR shifts the columns right and blanks come in at the left
convention ECMA-48 SR (xterm ctlseqs CSI Ps SP A, default 1) moves the data Ps columns right; here the columns between the margins of every line in the scrolling region move, and the cursor stays where it is
known-fail: alacritty – no SL or SR (CSI SP @, CSI SP A)
size 8 3
feed abcdefgh\r\nABCDEFGH\e[ A
screen
| abcdefg|
| ABCDEFG|

test SL and SR stay between the margins
convention SL and SR move only the columns between the margins (VT510 DECSLRM) and the rows of the scrolling region
known-fail: alacritty – no SL or SR (CSI SP @, CSI SP A)
size 8 3
feed abcdefgh\r\nABCDEFGH\e[?69h\e[3;6s\e[2;3r\e[1 @
screen
|abcdefgh|
|ABDEF GH|
cursor 1,1
feed \e[1 A
screen
|abcdefgh|
|AB DEFGH|

test SL erases with the background color
convention the cells that come in take the pen's background (bce), as every erase does
known-fail: alacritty – no SL or SR (CSI SP @, CSI SP A)
size 8 2
feed abcdefgh\e[44m\e[3 @
cell 1,8 bg=idx:4
cell 1,6 bg=idx:4
cell 1,5 bg=default
